(7148080, 1095262, 161988, '<td valign="top"><b><i>sfalice wrote "Someone did a fine job of composing this scene. You found it. Looks good!"</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi Alice,<br/> <br/>That "someone" would be me. (smile)  Thanks for the kind remarks about the photo.<br/> <br/>The background is actually a large mat with magnets on the back that we put on the front of our dishwasher every Christmas. My mother in law gave me the Santa on the motorcycle years ago because I ride a Harley. The "snow" was rolled cotton. I thought it looked cool, so I shot it.  All put together &amp; shot in my home studio.<br/> <br/>Best regards &amp; Happy New Year to you!<br/> <br/>Jay</td>', 'sfalice wrote "Someone did a fine job of composing this scene. You found it. Looks good!"  Hi Alice, That "someone" would be me. (smile)  Thanks for the kind remarks about the photo. The background is actually a large mat with magnets on the back that we put on the front of our dishwasher every Christmas. My mother in law gave me the Santa on the motorcycle years ago because I ride a Harley. The "snow" was rolled cotton. I thought it looked cool, so I shot it.  All put together & shot in my home studio. Best regards & Happy New Year to you! Jay', '2013-12-27 09:41:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(7148089, 1095641, 144365, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by vawendy:</b></div><hr/><i>I was bracketing, and two of the shots in the bracket were longerish exposures, so I kept thinking "don''t be blurry, don''t be blurry!" all the way home. :) </i></td></tr></table>Does that mean the duck wasn''t in all three exposures? Or at least in the same spot? <br/> <br/>Reminds me of this shot:<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=742853" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/945/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_742853.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/945/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_742853.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/945/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_742853.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>Your entry was my only ten of the challenge, but if the duck was traversing the scene and in a different location for each exposure, I don''t see how this can''t get DQ''ed given the precedence set before it. Without the duck in that exact location, I would have given this a four or five at best.</td>', 'Originally posted by vawendy:I was bracketing, and two of the shots in the bracket were longerish exposures, so I kept thinking "don''t be blurry, don''t be blurry!" all the way home. :) Does that mean the duck wasn''t in all three exposures? Or at least in the same spot?  Reminds me of this shot:  Your entry was my only ten of the challenge, but if the duck was traversing the scene and in a different location for each exposure, I don''t see how this can''t get DQ''ed given the precedence set before it. Without the duck in that exact location, I would have given this a four or five at best.', '2013-12-27 09:54:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(7148093, 1095070, 161988, '<td valign="top">Love the way you do Christmas at what I presume is your house.</td>', 'Love the way you do Christmas at what I presume is your house.', '2013-12-27 10:03:49.000000', NULL, 0),
