(7148194, 1095641, 103142, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by hahn23:</b></div><hr/><i> While it''s hard to say for sure the id of the waterfowl, my best guess, based on silhouette would be a Common Loon. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>We''ve never seen loons in our ponds, even though they winter in the tidewater region. It is probably a smaller than a loon or a cormorant, but was a kind of diving duck. It popped up in the reflection and dove again quickly. It was only in 3 frames before it dove.</td>', 'Originally posted by hahn23: While it''s hard to say for sure the id of the waterfowl, my best guess, based on silhouette would be a Common Loon.   We''ve never seen loons in our ponds, even though they winter in the tidewater region. It is probably a smaller than a loon or a cormorant, but was a kind of diving duck. It popped up in the reflection and dove again quickly. It was only in 3 frames before it dove.', '2013-12-27 12:57:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(7148195, 1095641, 103142, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by kasaba:</b></div><hr/><i>  although I have no idea what "time" this translates into for you :-). </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Got there about 6:15 and the shot was taken at about 6:50.<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by kasaba:  although I have no idea what "time" this translates into for you :-).   Got there about 6:15 and the shot was taken at about 6:50.', '2013-12-27 13:00:05.000000', NULL, 0),
