(7149472, 1095641, 66384, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by hahn23:</b></div><hr/><i> Congrats, vawendy, on your blue ribbon.  While it''s hard to say for sure the id of the waterfowl, my best guess, based on silhouette would be a Common Loon. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>In Florida we have grebes that look like this. They are diving birds. Their range extends up to VA, so perhaps that''s what you caught. Anyway, what I really wanted to say is this is a stunningly beautiful image. So peaceful!</td>', 'Originally posted by hahn23: Congrats, vawendy, on your blue ribbon.  While it''s hard to say for sure the id of the waterfowl, my best guess, based on silhouette would be a Common Loon.  In Florida we have grebes that look like this. They are diving birds. Their range extends up to VA, so perhaps that''s what you caught. Anyway, what I really wanted to say is this is a stunningly beautiful image. So peaceful!', '2013-12-30 12:10:51.000000', NULL, 0),
